{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 38","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of a certain rectangular solid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb08ef23c9e1ffb28dca4066950b6d23e383876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216\\text{ cm}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, its total surface area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d616b128343b37c4db403405d37615a870df73c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288\\text{ cm}^2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, and its three dimensions are in \ngeometric progression. Find the sum of the lengths in cm of all the edges of this solid.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the three side lengths be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/558702f1b2093199b14d226c30e5c69a644f00e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{a}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18badee7e76fa5812c3dd04f83ef07963fd9b33e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ar$\" width=\"17\" height=\"8\" />.  Because the volume of the solid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb08ef23c9e1ffb28dca4066950b6d23e383876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216\\text{ cm}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea8e3a7271194f085ddf3111ef83ff92b69089d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{r} \\cdot a \\cdot ar = 216\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d0baaa3c91d45e65dd8de5ca5c32e1a688b22b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 6\\]\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\nThe surface area of the solid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d616b128343b37c4db403405d37615a870df73c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288\\text{ cm}^2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ce05dbf1d0388922b167b2aab15bdad23f2cb1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(\\frac{a^2}{r} + a^2r + a^2) = 288\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"39\" />\nNote that the sum of the side lengths of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b10fdedd1a1c10778ffbc89d3548b6ff362681d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(\\tfrac{6}{r} + 6 + 6r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"103\" height=\"21\" /> and that the equation above has a similar form.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995dd27cb549a8b4d3d9109bca6a738de55f2831.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(\\frac{36}{r} + 36r + 36) = 288\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca8222bd605214c646b75bdb0c6a2cc6f67b5521.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(\\frac{6}{r} + 6r + 6) = 48\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c681af118d5cf983b4ee8877bed9b41cfd9934de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4(\\frac{6}{r} + 6r + 6) = 96\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" />\nThe sum of all the edges of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d6e4aeabafb54bd3d7e9bbe1e930d1b7b901d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> centimeters.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_37\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 37\">Problem 37</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 39\">Problem 39</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> 